{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483180-do-you-think-paradox-should-read-what-we-write-on-here","id":1483180,"title":"Do you think Paradox should read what we write on here?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-05T15:28:06-07:00","id":1483180,"title":"Do you think Paradox should read what we write on here?","content":"We post a lot of different things related to VTM on this forum. With the amount of theories, debates, arguments, and even information on lore and powers that are unknown to many, it seems like a treasure trove of information that would be useful to paradox when they create their next VTM game, whether it be an interactive fiction or a videogame. Maybe they can get a bit more involved and have Q&amp;A sessions to shed light on questions the players may have for team working on the game.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm wrong. Perhaps what we want or find interesting, isn't the same as what most people want or find interesting. Perhaps our opinions are more harmful than helpful. It's possible that the current path the company has chosen, is the best path to take.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T15:50:24-07:00","id":1483181,"title":"","content":"Paradox is attempting to maximize their ESG Score, so no, they will not be taking our suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T17:26:44-07:00","id":1483194,"title":"","content":"Well, it could be a similar situation to writing for a show or book series. You can't, or more accurately shouldn't, view fan made content. There is a legal reason, and a narrative reason for this BTW. Legally it's to help avoid copyright/trademark issues. We humans take information we have observed and naturally remix it when we create anything. This is an issue for writing as it can cause accidently problems with plagiarism and such, or at least the accusation of such things. As such, many writers for ongoing projects will willingly, or be obligated contractually, to avoid fan content so they can have some plausible deniability if a coincidence does happen.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if writers see feedback or a theory that is almost 100% what you were planning to do, the writer's naturally reaction is to change it in order to maintain an element of twist in the story. Obviously, this often makes a story feel cheap, just look at recent Star Wars and the Game of Thrones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T18:13:38-07:00","id":1483196,"title":"","content":"We tried speculating on whether Bloodlines 2 would even come out and the thread had to be closed because a sad puppy kept bringing up identity politics.<br /> <br /> No offense but if Paradox did have someone reading these forums, I hope they give them hazard pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T19:56:15-07:00","id":1483202,"title":"","content":"Near as I can tell Paradox didn't even read the playtest feedback for V5, they're not going to be reading the forums of the company they are currently actively cutting out of future product development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T20:39:44-07:00","id":1483204,"title":"","content":"I think Paradox <i>should</i> listen to what people here say, but we're just a bunch of grognards so what do we know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T02:38:37-07:00","id":1483207,"title":"","content":"WoD is now a mainstream product owned by a large corporation who is obviously focused on maximizing their profits, why should they listen to the fans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T05:01:53-07:00","id":1483210,"title":"","content":"Well they don't listen to their own fanbase so....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T08:59:36-07:00","id":1483222,"title":"","content":"I get the reputation as the 5th Edition guy but if I was Paradox, I would just hand over the tabletop RPG development to Onyx Path and hook them up with a decent mass printer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T09:10:09-07:00","id":1483224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483180-do-you-think-paradox-should-read-what-we-write-on-here?p=1483202#post1483202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Near as I can tell Paradox didn't even read the playtest feedback for V5, they're not going to be reading the forums of the company they are currently actively cutting out of future product development.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one thing they changed was the only 3 attributes thing, raising it to 9 once again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T10:45:04-07:00","id":1483230,"title":"","content":"So, to paraphrase someone that I don't feel like citing because he can get attention from someone else:<br /> <br /> Fans - as a group - are great at noticing when something isn't right, but horrible at telling you what's wrong.<br /> <br /> That's why I think the OP was right to phrase it as &quot;read.&quot; Yeah, Paradox should have someone that's reading stuff here. People don't talk about these things so much if they didn't care about them. If they care about them, they're a resources for increasing profits because we're cheap labor. Again, the whole point of the reference above, is not to just do what we say; the fans as a collective highlighting something that needs work doesn't mean you take sides in the debates on how to fix it based on forum arguments. You get your designers to focus on that topic and see what they can do; that's what you hired them to do. If you're even mediocre at iterative design, your game gets better in a fashion that increases sales.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean you're going to make everyone a fan of the game in the end, just maximize from the pool of potential fans. &quot;Not the change I would have made, but I'm glad they did something here,&quot; goes a long way with a lot of people that are on the fence about a product. You maybe shift a few people on the &quot;still nope&quot; side of the fence to the &quot;maybe&quot; fence sitters too, and then some future iteration gets them to buy.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way: you build goodwill with your fans by using the huge amount of free research into what areas of your game need adjustments to show that you are listening to the fans, and then finding solutions. They don't have to be groundbreaking. They don't have to even work all that well. Trying shows acknowledgement, and a willingness to expand the game (aka appeal to more people and get more sales!) rather than be overly dogmatic to one vision of what the game should be.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest corporate-level mistakes I think Paradox made when buying the WoD/etc. IPs from CCP, was letting the WoD fans in their ranks confuse brand loyalty and company goodwill. CCP kept a lot of goodwill from the oWW because they kept a lot of the current oWW people on staff during the buyout. Our favorite development teams weren't getting canned for new ones with the new company. We could trust that, at least for awhile, the products would be the same even with some hiccups in the transition. Yeah, this lead to some silly things like CCP hating the idea of a new &quot;edition&quot; of the CofD instead of just patching it like you would a video game. But pretty much right up until they cancelled the WoDMMO and then canned most of the oWW holdovers, the fans had a decent amount of goodwill towards CCP for letting the oWW games continue on as best as possible in a new economic reality.<br /> <br /> Paradox really boggled that process. They were in a goodwill deficit before they got a single RPG book out, because they leaned way too heavily on brand loyalty, and didn't consider that they had done nothing to establish goodwill. Ever since Paradox ending the nWW as its own subsidiary, it's clear they've been trying to reverse that. There's been a lot more attention to community outreach (even if not here), there's been some shifts that at least show that they recognize some of the early mistakes they made. But if they want to keep that trend going, they need to pay attention to what people are saying. Again, not to do what someone like me says is the best thing to do, but because a couple people like me harping on the same things over and over is a reason to say, &quot;Do they have a point? If so, can we do something about it that doesn't make five other things worse?&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> Even with D&amp;D in your equations, the TTRPG industry is a tiny niche luxury market. There isn't enough money in it to do the kind of market research for future products like Samsung or Ford can afford to do. But TTRPG fans are also willing to talk endlessly about TTRPG in public spaces, meaning you don't need to do traditional market research: you just need a couple designers that can translate fan discourse into actionable design changes that lead to a better overall product.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T11:15:00-07:00","id":1483235,"title":"","content":"I'd just be happy with Paradox letting OP do &quot;Legacy&quot; content for WOD, like their planned 4th edition etc. Basically I would love for a Pathfinder version of WOD. More power to people who love V5, its just not my cup of tea and loved the stuff OP was putting out for the V20 line. Yes, I know there is the STV. Which is cool, but not the same to me. I don't know, seems like a good way to maximize your profits off an IP to just give everyone what they want at the same time. Imagine if Wizards did D&amp;D and Pathfinder. They would have gotten both revenue streams. Just my thoughts anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T13:10:44-07:00","id":1483246,"title":"","content":"read? Maybe, use as gospel, hell no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T11:59:07-07:00","id":1483322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483180-do-you-think-paradox-should-read-what-we-write-on-here?p=1483222#post1483222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the reputation as the 5th Edition guy but if I was Paradox, I would just hand over the tabletop RPG development to Onyx Path and hook them up with a decent mass printer.</div> </div> </div> </div>To get back to a point here:<br /> <br /> Paradox, by virtue of increasing the profitability of Exalted and the CofD alone, should be hooking Onyx Path up with a different resource (because I'm fairly confident that if Rich thought he could sell a 50k print run to justify getting a deal with a bigger printer he still has the connections to do that): translation partners to get the books out in more languages and thus to more people.<br /> <br /> While Onyx Path would never skyrocket back into where oWW was with that alone, we know there are large WoD fanbases in countries were English isn't the primary language. Onyx Path doesn't have the resources to get regular and timely translation into the big languages in countries we know have a large TTRPG market. We frequently get posters here that aren't native English speakers and have questions that they might not have if they could get books in their native tongue (or at least a much more frequently used one). Even if with, say, a two year delay, I can't help but imagine that if all the X20 books were out in Portuguese, Spanish, French, and German alone, it would probably have seen a very significant increase in sales.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T14:05:20-07:00","id":1483333,"title":"","content":"So, yes, they should read the threads here. And yes, they should also ignore a lot of it.<br /> <br /> Sifting the good from the bad is a fine art. Some ideas we have are good, others are less good, and some are just awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T14:37:51-07:00","id":1483337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483180-do-you-think-paradox-should-read-what-we-write-on-here?p=1483322#post1483322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To get back to a point here:<br /> <br /> Paradox, by virtue of increasing the profitability of Exalted and the CofD alone, should be hooking Onyx Path up with a different resource (because I'm fairly confident that if Rich thought he could sell a 50k print run to justify getting a deal with a bigger printer he still has the connections to do that): translation partners to get the books out in more languages and thus to more people.<br /> <br /> While Onyx Path would never skyrocket back into where oWW was with that alone, we know there are large WoD fanbases in countries were English isn't the primary language. Onyx Path doesn't have the resources to get regular and timely translation into the big languages in countries we know have a large TTRPG market. We frequently get posters here that aren't native English speakers and have questions that they might not have if they could get books in their native tongue (or at least a much more frequently used one). Even if with, say, a two year delay, I can't help but imagine that if all the X20 books were out in Portuguese, Spanish, French, and German alone, it would probably have seen a very significant increase in sales.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fuck yeah, I own the whole 2nd edition line and a good chunk of 1st ed supplements, I would buy everything again if they translated them in my language, finding new players is a struggle because the books are written in a fairly complex English and many of my potential players gave up, I don't think Onyx Path understands how popular CoD really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T15:10:27-07:00","id":1483339,"title":"","content":"Something else that I think is beneficial for game writing that's not a directly about Paradox? IME explaining things to help translators find a good phrasing in the language they're working on, can help you with your own phrasing in your native language. Scion 2e's language is frequently seen as hard to interpret, and I can see how the process of explaining things where just certain turns of phrase don't work could have helped refine the book a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T09:25:54-07:00","id":1483382,"title":"","content":"This maybe paranoia talking here, but how do we know that they don't? If I ran a multinational company with solid funds, I would hire people to look over any and all social media mentioning the company's IP, just to make sure that the brand isn't being used the wrong way. The possibility of using the information found there to improve a product would be secondary, but potentially useful. That might actually be a good job for some people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T10:59:32-07:00","id":1483387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483180-do-you-think-paradox-should-read-what-we-write-on-here?p=1483382#post1483382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This maybe paranoia talking here, but how do we know that they don't? If I ran a multinational company with solid funds, I would hire people to look over any and all social media mentioning the company's IP, just to make sure that the brand isn't being used the wrong way. The possibility of using the information found there to improve a product would be secondary, but potentially useful. That might actually be a good job for some people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think paradox cares enough to do that. But who knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T13:12:54-07:00","id":1483398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483180-do-you-think-paradox-should-read-what-we-write-on-here?p=1483337#post1483337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I don't think Onyx Path understands how popular CoD really is.</div> </div> </div> </div>To go back a bit, again:<br /> <br /> I don't think this is directly under Onyx Path's control. I can't say this for certain, but to the best of my knowledge, Onyx Path doesn't have a license to get the books they make for WoD/Exalted/CofD translated. So they would either have to pay Paradox even more money for the rights to then hire people to do the localization process, or see if Paradox will do it themselves.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path people have confirmed similar issues in the past. And Onyx Path, alone, is still a small company with pretty slim margins; there's just no feasible way for them to do that on their own even if Paradox gave them permission to without additional licensing fees. If you consider that we're talking about an effort that would probably amount to something like a $5K Kickstarter drive, per book, per language (kind averaging out a bit since different sized books would obviously not cost the same, and I'm probably low balling the cost) just for PoD quality books at that, I can see why Onyx Path's math is to stick to English for now.<br /> <br /> That's why I put the onus on Paradox in my original post: they have the resources (not just money) to make this happen. They could make it happen even if Onyx Path didn't want to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483180-do-you-think-paradox-should-read-what-we-write-on-here?p=1483382#post1483382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This maybe paranoia talking here, but how do we know that they don't?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) In theory they kinda do. Onyx Path is a licensed partner of Paradox, so anything that goes on here is read by people that &quot;work&quot; for Paradox on some level. The problem is that only really applies to what you're talking about<b></b>: keeping an eye out for IP abuses. It doesn't get into the issues of actually utilizing the chatter here as a positive resource.<br /> <br /> 2) It's extremely hard to police using a brand &quot;the wrong way,&quot; online when it existed for ~25 years before you bought it. There's just too much stuff out there that was allowed by the oWW, and CCP, that trying to police it would just be a massive headache, make the fans hate you, and very likely cost far more money than it could possibly generate. There's a reason why a lot of companies don't actively fight piracy as much as they used to. They'll stop the most flagrant stuff, but the costs of enforcement are really high, and the benefits of enforcement are pretty low. Paying someone ~$30K to stop ~10K in net loss just doesn't make sense. So you eat the loss. It's not optimal by any means, but it's where a lot of RPG companies are.<br /> <br /> And that's just stuff a company can do anything about. If someone posts Instagram pics of themselves, and their Brujah Clan tattoo, while bragging about petty crimes they do to stick it to The Man... what is Paradox going to really do about that? Sue for defamation?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T22:07:51-07:00","id":1483443,"title":"","content":"I think a 5k Kickstart would at most cover the PDF version of a single book, given the costs with translation, editing and layout (it must be entirely revised with the new text), plus sourcing a local sale, which is another relevant step.<br /> <br /> Selling for other countries isn't just translating to their language, but also simplifying the process, as buying from another country, in another currency, isn't that simple. You must deal with exchange rates and taxes for them, at the very least, and possibly with other legal requirements. It isn't rocket science nowadays, but is something you must do if the translation effort isn't to be wasted, and will have a cost.<br /> <br /> Yet, I definitely think it is worth it, but for now the fact is that Paradox simply isn't doing it, and without them that's a no deal for OPP alone.<br /> <br /> As for why do we think they're not reading here? Mostly I just don't have this impression, but it is perfectly possible they are. Reading isn't posting, though. For companies there are many, many considerations to be taken before you create an active account on any platform, as that will be a part of their public image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T08:14:34-07:00","id":1483590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483180-do-you-think-paradox-should-read-what-we-write-on-here?p=1483443#post1483443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a 5k Kickstart would at most cover the PDF version of a single book, given the costs with translation, editing and layout (it must be entirely revised with the new text), plus sourcing a local sale, which is another relevant step.<br /> <br /> Selling for other countries isn't just translating to their language, but also simplifying the process, as buying from another country, in another currency, isn't that simple. You must deal with exchange rates and taxes for them, at the very least, and possibly with other legal requirements. It isn't rocket science nowadays, but is something you must do if the translation effort isn't to be wasted, and will have a cost.<br /> <br /> Yet, I definitely think it is worth it, but for now the fact is that Paradox simply isn't doing it, and without them that's a no deal for OPP alone.<br /> <br /> As for why do we think they're not reading here? Mostly I just don't have this impression, but it is perfectly possible they are. Reading isn't posting, though. For companies there are many, many considerations to be taken before you create an active account on any platform, as that will be a part of their public image.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Paradox will never invest in CoD when they spent a lot on WoD already, I also doubt they bother to read the forums given the fact that they haven't fixed none of the issues that the fans have been pointing out since day one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}